{"nodes": [{"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_document", "label": "Long Side-question Conversations and the Context Budget (English)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_output_budget", "label": "Independent Side-question Output Budget", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defaults to at most 8192 output tokens and never exceeds the output limit already set in the main configuration; ARTEX_BTW_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS can set 256-32768 without changing the product's default model or main-task parameters. This replaces inheriting the main task's 32K output reservation."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_input_budget", "label": "Input Budget and Safety Margin", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Input budget = context window minus the output limit minus a safety margin of 5% of the window (clamped to 128..8192 tokens); when the window size is unknown the platform default of 200K is used. Verbatim recent Q&A is capped at one quarter of this input budget and at most 16K."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_rolling_summary", "label": "Rolling Summary of Older Q&A", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Successful Q&A is reloaded in increasing ordinal order, up to 20 exchanges verbatim; Q&A beyond the token budget is folded into a rolling summary carrying the source record and context time point. Past assistant answers are not new tool evidence, so the latest main snapshot wins conflicts."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_compaction", "label": "Background Preparation and Compaction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "POST accepts and returns the request first, then preparation and compaction run in the background without holding the admission lock or a database transaction. SSE and history expose preparation, Q&A consolidation, copy compaction, and response phases; a compaction failure becomes the request's failed terminal state."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_overflow_recovery", "label": "Single Context-overflow Recovery", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only the first context-overflow error triggers recovery, only before any text or tool call has been emitted, and only one retry is allowed; recovery stops immediately if the estimated size does not decrease. Other model errors and partially streamed output never trigger it."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_usage_accounting", "label": "Cumulative Usage Accounting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All usage already accumulated, including summarization, failed attempts, and usage at cancellation, is added to the same side-question request. If the Provider returns no usage only 0 is recorded, and estimates are never presented as actual usage."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_char_count_regression", "label": "Character-count-as-token Regression", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The previous implementation treated the request JSON's character count as the token count and inherited the main task's 32K output reservation, so it rejected legitimate side questions in advance whenever there was a lot of HTML, JS, or tool output. The revision on 2026-09-11 introduced an independent output budget and safer token estimation."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_summary_cache", "label": "Snapshot-scoped Summary Cache", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Main-context summaries are cached per snapshot identity in side_question_sessions.memory. A summary is saved only while the original request still runs and the cleanup version matches; Clear wipes the cache, a late write cannot revive cleared data, and a new snapshot never reuses the previous snapshot's summary."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_norma_estimation", "label": "norma UTF-8 Byte Token Estimation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Messages use norma's method of estimating UTF-8 bytes per content block plus a 4/3 margin, with system prompt, tool schema, and message-wrapping overhead counted additionally. This is an estimate, not the model's exact token count."}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_grok_cli", "label": "Grok CLI Side-question Implementation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/superagent-ai/grok-cli/blob/fb97af83f06dca873281d60168430f06c8de6324/src/utils/side-question.ts", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_opencode", "label": "OpenCode Session Compaction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/b3f1a96c6dd7adeb28b36dd11add1998fc84d67b/packages/core/src/session/compaction.ts", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "sidequestion_context_budget_norma", "label": "norma (v0.3.6 / v0.3.7)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The README targets norma v0.3.7 while the context-budget and validation documents record v0.3.6; ARTEX keeps norma's structured messages and tool pairing as-is rather than modifying norma sources."}], "edges": [{"source": "sidequestion_context_budget_char_count_regression", "target": "sidequestion_context_budget_output_budget", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sidequestion_context_budget_output_budget", "target": "sidequestion_context_budget_input_budget", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sidequestion_context_budget_input_budget", "target": "sidequestion_context_budget_norma_estimation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sidequestion_context_budget_norma_estimation", "target": "sidequestion_context_budget_norma", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "sidequestion/CONTEXT_BUDGET.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "sidequestion_context_budget_input_budget", "target": "si